# Product Requirements Document (PRD): Loan User Management Microservice

## 1. Overview

The Loan User Management Microservice is a Java 21 Spring Boot application that provides APIs for managing users and their associated loans. The system will use an in-memory database for data storage and will provide comprehensive documentation through Swagger UI.

## 2. Objectives

- Create a robust microservice architecture for managing loan users
- Implement complete CRUD operations for both users and loans
- Allow users to be associated with multiple loans
- Track user Out-Of-Office (OOO) status
- Provide functionality for transferring loans between users
- Ensure comprehensive API documentation through Swagger UI
- Include sample data generation for testing purposes

## 3. Functional Requirements

### 3.1 User Management
- Create new users with personal information and OOO status
- Retrieve user details by ID or username
- Update existing user information
- Delete users from the system
- Count total number of users in the system
- Check if a user exists by ID or username
- Check if a user is Out-Of-Office (OOO)

### 3.2 Loan Management
- Create new loans with appropriate details
- Associate loans with specific users
- Retrieve loan details by ID or other search criteria
- Update existing loan information
- Delete loans from the system
- Count total number of loans in the system
- Check if a specific loan exists
- Transfer loans from one user to another

### 3.3 User-Loan Relationship
- Users can be assigned to multiple loans
- Loans can be transferred between users
- System must maintain the integrity of user-loan relationships

## 4. Technical Requirements

### 4.1 Architecture
- Spring Boot microservice architecture
- RESTful API design
- In-memory database (H2) for data storage
- Swagger UI for API documentation

### 4.2 Technology Stack
- Java 21
- Spring Boot 3.x
- Spring Data JPA
- H2 Database
- OpenAPI/Swagger for documentation
- JUnit and MockMvc for testing

### 4.3 Data Models

**User Entity:**
- ID (Primary Key)
- Username (Unique)
- First Name
- Last Name
- Email
- Phone Number
- OOO Status (Boolean)
- Creation Date
- List of associated loans

**Loan Entity:**
- ID (Primary Key)
- Loan Number (Unique)
- Amount
- Interest Rate
- Term (in months)
- Start Date
- Status (Active, Closed, Pending)
- User Reference

## 5. API Endpoints

### 5.1 User APIs
- `POST /api/users` - Create a new user
- `GET /api/users` - Get all users
- `GET /api/users/{id}` - Get user by ID
- `GET /api/users/username/{username}` - Get user by username
- `PUT /api/users/{id}` - Update a user
- `DELETE /api/users/{id}` - Delete a user
- `GET /api/users/count` - Get total count of users
- `GET /api/users/exists/{id}` - Check if user exists by ID
- `GET /api/users/exists/username/{username}` - Check if user exists by username
- `GET /api/users/{id}/ooo` - Check if user is OOO by ID
- `GET /api/users/username/{username}/ooo` - Check if user is OOO by username

### 5.2 Loan APIs
- `POST /api/loans` - Create a new loan
- `GET /api/loans` - Get all loans
- `GET /api/loans/{id}` - Get loan by ID
- `PUT /api/loans/{id}` - Update a loan
- `DELETE /api/loans/{id}` - Delete a loan
- `GET /api/loans/count` - Get total count of loans
- `GET /api/loans/exists/{id}` - Check if loan exists

### 5.3 User-Loan APIs
- `POST /api/users/{userId}/loans` - Add a loan to a user
- `GET /api/users/{userId}/loans` - Get all loans for a user
- `POST /api/loans/transfer` - Transfer loans between users by username

## 6. Sample Data

- System will be pre-populated with 10 sample users
- Some users will have OOO status set to true
- Each sample user will have 10 associated loans
- Total of 100 sample loans will be created for testing

## 7. Non-Functional Requirements

### 7.1 Performance
- API response times should be under 200ms
- System should handle concurrent requests efficiently

### 7.2 Security
- Basic input validation to prevent injection attacks

### 7.3 Documentation
- Comprehensive API documentation with Swagger UI
- Clear request/response examples
- Required parameters and response codes documented

## 8. Acceptance Criteria

- All API endpoints function as specified
- Sample data is correctly generated, including some users with OOO status
- Swagger UI provides comprehensive API documentation
- All CRUD operations for both users and loans work correctly
- User OOO status can be checked
- Loan transfer functionality works as specified
- In-memory database correctly maintains relationships between entities

## 9. Constraints

- The system will use an in-memory database, so data persistence is limited to application runtime
- The system is designed as a standalone microservice without external dependencies